The argument to a function is formed by one or more of  the  val‐
ues: The flag requests receipt of out‐of‐band data that would not
be  received in the normal data stream.  Some protocols place ex‐
pedited data at the head of the normal data queue, and thus  this
flag cannot be used with such protocols.  The flag causes the re‐
ceive  operation to return data from the beginning of the receive
queue without removing that data from the queue.  Thus, a  subse‐
quent  receive call will return the same data.  The flag requests
that the operation block until the  full  request  is  satisfied.
